	"title"			"Multi-Select Tool for macOS (arm64)"
	"description"		"Rectangle multi-select and group movement for Two Point Museum on Apple Silicon.\n\nHold Left Shift, drag a rectangle, release: the group follows the cursor. Left click places it, right click cancels and restores the original positions.\n\nmacOS does NOT need BepInEx or any .NET runtime, and the game bundle is never modified: the mod is a dylib injected with DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES.\n\nHOW TO USE\n1. Subscribe to this item and let Steam download it.\n2. Set the game's Steam launch options to:\n   bash \"<Steam>/steamapps/workshop/content/2185060/<THIS ITEM ID>/run_tpm.sh\" %command%\n   (replace <Steam> with your Steam library path)\n   Alternatively copy run_tpm.sh anywhere and point the launch options at it; the script finds the dylib next to itself or in the workshop folder.\n3. Launch the game normally and use Left Shift + drag.\n\nLogs: /tmp/tpm_ms_native.log\n\nRequires an Apple Silicon Mac and macOS 13+. Intel Macs are not supported.\n\nSource and issues: https://github.com/Dywane/tpm-mac-multiselect\n"
	"changenote"		"1.0.0 - first release"
}
